# Scaling & jobs backlog

When you **defer**, **decide against for launch**, or **discover** a future need related to:

- job queues / Redis / workers / multi-replica
- extraction architecture (chunking, parallel OCR/LLM, reconcile)
- page/file/token limits that will change later
- OpenAI/cost metering ops beyond current in-process estimates
- orphan runs, retries, TTL cleanup, capacity triggers

…you **must** update [`docs/SCALING-AND-JOBS.md`](docs/SCALING-AND-JOBS.md) in the **same change**.

## Do

- Add a short row or subsection: **current behavior**, **why deferred**, **trigger to build**, **preferred approach** if known.
- Keep launch posture tables accurate when you ship a new guardrail (e.g. max pages/file).
- Prefer editing SCALING-AND-JOBS over leaving “later” only in chat or NEXT-STEPS.

## Don’t

- Ship a “we’ll chunk later” / “when we scale…” comment in code without a matching SCALING-AND-JOBS note.
- Put Redis/worker/chunking implementation detail only in NEXT-STEPS — that file is near-term product ship; scaling backlog lives here.
